<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Momentum Life sees slower 2nd half growth.</title>
<headline>Momentum Life sees slower 2nd half growth.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Momentum Life Assurers Ltd said on Thursday it expected slower earnings growth in the second half since the impact of the turnaround at Aegis will be less significant in the next six months.</p>
<p>&quot;However, the board is confident that the group is well positioned to show satisfactory growth for the full financial year,&quot; the company said in a statement with half year results.</p>
<p>Attributable net taxed surplus jumped to 83.5 million rand in the first half from 46.6 million, helped by a strong improvement at Aegis where Momentum's share of profits jumped to 6.4 million rand from a loss of 7.5 million.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
